Let $\alpha \in (0, 1)$, and suppose Condition ef{cond:sum} is satisfied. For every $n$ and every $j = 1, \hdots, k$ let $\hat{
u}^2_{j,n} \geq 0$ be an estimator of $\mathbb{V}_n(r_n^{(j)})$, and let $\hat{K}_n \geq 0$ be an estimator of $K_{1-\alpha}(\corr(\mathbb{V}_n(r_n)))$, so that the sequence  egin{equation*} \kappa_n =  rac{K_{1-\alpha}(\corr(\mathbb{V}_n(r_n)))}{\hat{K}_n} \max_{j = 1, \hdots, k} \sqrt{ rac{[\mathbb{V}_n(r_n)]_{j} }{ \hat{
u}^2_{j,n} }}, \end{equation*} satisfies  egin{equation} \mathbb{P}_n \left( \kappa_n \geq 1+ \eps ight) 	o 0 	ext{ for every } \eps > 0, \end{equation} (implicitly including that $\mathbb{P}_n(\kappa_n 	ext{ is well defined} ) 	o 1$) or, equivalently, that the condition in \eqref{eqn:asptup} holds with $\kappa_n$ replaced by  egin{equation*}  rac{K_{1-\alpha}(\corr(S_n))}{\hat{K}_n} \max_{j = 1, \hdots, k} \sqrt{ rac{[S_n]_{j} }{ \hat{
u}^2_{j,n} }}. \end{equation*} For every $\mathbb{M} \in \mathsf{M}_n$ and every $j = 1, \hdots, m(\mathbb{M})$, define the confidence interval  egin{equation*} \mathrm{CI}_{1 - \alpha, \mathbb{M}}^{(j), \mathrm{oest}} \quad = \quad \hat{	heta}^{(j)}_{\mathbb{M}, n} \pm \sqrt{\hat{
u}^2_{ho(\M) + j, n}} ~ \hat{K}_n. \end{equation*} Then, for every (measurable) model selection procedure $\hat{\mathbb{M}}_n$, we have  egin{equation*} \liminf_{n 	o \infty} \mathbb{P}_n \left( 	heta_{\hat{\mathbb{M}}_n, n}^{*(j)} \in \mathrm{CI}_{1 - \alpha, \hat{\mathbb{M}}_n}^{(j), \mathrm{oest}} 	ext{ for all } j = 1, \hdots, m(\hat{\mathbb{M}}_n) ight) \geq 1-\alpha. \end{equation*} In the important special case where $\hat{K}_n \geq K_{1-\alpha}(\corr(\mathbb{V}_n(r_n)))$ holds eventually, the condition in Equation \eqref{eqn:asptup} is implied by the condition that for every $j = 1, \hdots, k$ it holds that  egin{equation} \mathbb{P}_n \left( \sqrt{ rac{[S_n]_{j} }{ \hat{
u}^2_{j,n} }} \geq 1+ \eps ight) 	o 0 	ext{ for every } \eps > 0, \end{equation} or equivalently, that for every $j = 1, \hdots, k$ it holds that  egin{equation} \mathbb{P}_n \left( \sqrt{ rac{[\mathbb{V}_n(r_n)]_{j} }{ \hat{
u}^2_{j,n} }} \geq 1+ \eps ight) 	o 0 	ext{ for every } \eps > 0. \end{equation}

The proof is a variation of the consistency part of the proof of Theorem~4 in \citet{Fahrmeir90}. Fix $n$ large enough, such that the bound of Condition~ef{cond:X2}\eqref{cX2:Huber} holds, the pseudo parameter of Lemma~ef{lemma:pseudo} exists and the bound of Lemma~ef{lemma:pseudoBound} applies. Fix $\M\in\mathsf{M}_n$ and $\P_n\in\mathbf{P}_n^{(\mathrm{bin})}(	au)$, write $ eta_{\M,n}^* =  eta_{\M,n}^*(\P_n)$ and note that by Condition~ef{cond:H}\eqref{cH:C2}, the function $ eta\mapsto \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta)$ is twice continuously differentiable on $\R^{m(\M)}$ and thus, for every $y\in\{0,1\}^n$, admits the expansion  egin{align*} \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta) \quad&=\quad \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta_{\M,n}^*) \;+\; ( eta- eta_{\M,n}^*)'U_{M,n}^{1/2}U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(y) \ &\quad-\;  rac{1}{2}( eta- eta_{\M,n}^*)'U_{M,n}^{1/2}U_{M,n}^{-1/2}H_{\M,n}(y,	ilde{ eta}_n)U_{M,n}^{-1/2}U_{M,n}^{1/2}( eta- eta_{\M,n}^*), \end{align*} for some $	ilde{ eta}_n\in\{a eta + (1-a) eta_{\M,n}^* : a\in[0,1]\}$, and where $s_{\M,n}^*(y) =  rac{\partial \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta)}{\partial  eta}\Big|_{ eta= eta_{\M,n}^*}$, $H_{\M,n}(y, eta) = - rac{\partial \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta)}{\partial eta\partial eta'}$, and $U_{M,n} = X_n[M]'X_n[M]/n$. For $\delta>0$, define $\lambda_n = \sqrt{n}U_{M,n}^{1/2}( eta- eta_{\M.n}^*)/\delta$ to rewrite the previous equation as  egin{align*} \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta) \;-\; \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta_{\M,n}^*) \;&=\; \delta \lambda_n'U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(y)/\sqrt{n} \ &\quad-\;  rac{1}{2}\delta^2 \lambda_n'U_{M,n}^{-1/2}(H_{\M,n}(y,	ilde{ eta}_n)/n)U_{M,n}^{-1/2}\lambda_n, \end{align*} for all $ eta\in\R^{m(\M)}$ and all $y\in\{0,1\}^n$. For $N_n(\delta) := N_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)$ as in Lemma~ef{lemma:Hcontinuity}ef{l:Hcont:B}, define $ L_n(y,\delta) := \inf_{ eta\in N_n(\delta)} \lmin\left(U_{M,n}^{-1/2}(H_{\M,n}(y, eta)/n)U_{M,n}^{-1/2}ight), $ take $ eta\in\partial N_n(\delta) = \{ eta\in\R^{m(\M)} : \|\sqrt{n}U_{M,n}^{1/2}( eta- eta_{\M,n}^*)\|= \delta\}$ and observe that now $\|\lambda_n\|=1$, $\delta\lambda_n'U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(y)/\sqrt{n} \le \delta \|U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(y)/\sqrt{n}\|$ and  egin{align*}  rac{1}{2}\delta^2 L_n(y,\delta) \;&\le\;  rac{1}{2}\delta^2 \lmin\left(U_{M,n}^{-1/2}(H_{\M,n}(y,	ilde{ eta})/n)U_{M,n}^{-1/2}ight) \ \;&\le\;  rac{1}{2}\delta^2 \lambda_n'U_{M,n}^{-1/2}(H_{\M,n}(y,	ilde{ eta})/n)U_{M,n}^{-1/2}\lambda_n, \end{align*} for all $y\in\{0,1\}^n$. Therefore, we have the inclusion  egin{align*} E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta) &:= \{y\in\{0,1\}^n:\delta\|U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(y)/\sqrt{n}\| < \delta^2 L_n(y,\delta)/2\} \ &\subseteq \{y\in\{0,1\}^n :  orall  eta\in\partial N_n(\delta) : \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta) < \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta_{\M,n}^*)\} =: F_n(\delta). \end{align*} As a consequence, for every $y \in E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)$, the function $ eta\mapsto \ell_{\M,n}(y, eta)$ has a local maximum $\hat{ eta}_{\M,n}(y)$ on the interior of $N_n(\delta)$. By strict concavity (Conditions~ef{cond:H}\eqref{cH:concave} and ef{cond:X2}\eqref{cX2:rank}), this is a unique global maximum. Moreover, we have $F_n(\delta) \subseteq \{y: \hat{ eta}_{\M,n}(y) \in N_n(\delta)\} = \{y: \|\sqrt{n}U_{M,n}^{1/2}(\hat{ eta}_{\M,n}(y) -  eta_{\M,n}^*)\| \le \delta\}$. Hence, $$ \P_n(\|\sqrt{n}U_{M,n}^{1/2}(\hat{ eta}_{\M,n}(y) -  eta_{\M,n}^*)\| > \delta) \;\le\; \P_n(E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)^c). $$ It remains to verify that $\P_n(E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)^c)$ is small for large $n$, uniformly in $\M$ and $\P_n$. Take $\eps>0$ and note that  egin{align} \P_n(E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)^c) \;&\le\; 
otag \P_n(4\|U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(\cdot)/\sqrt{n}\|^2\ge \delta^2 L_n^2(\cdot,\delta), L_n^2(\cdot,\delta) \ge \eps^2 ) 
otag\ &\;\quad\;+\; \P_n(L_n^2(\cdot,\delta) < \eps^2 ) \ &\le \; \P_n(4\|U_{M,n}^{-1/2}s_{\M,n}^*(\cdot)/\sqrt{n}\|^2\ge \delta^2 \eps^2) \;+\; \P_n(L_n^2(\cdot,\delta) < \eps^2 )
otag\ &\le \; 4 rac{	race(U_{M,n}^{-1/2}\VC_n(s_{\M,n}^*/\sqrt{n})U_{M,n}^{-1/2})}{\delta^2\eps^2} \;+\; \P_n(L_n(\cdot,\delta) < \eps ), 
otag \end{align} in view of Markov's inequality and since $\E_n[s_{\M,n}^*] = 0$. Note that $\VC_n(s_{\M,n}^*) = X_n[M]'V_{\M,\P_n,n}^*X_n[M]$, for a diagonal matrix $V_{\M,\P_n,n}^*$ whose diagonal entries satisfy  egin{align*} [V_{\M,\P_n,n}^*]_{ii} \;&=\; \P_{i,n}(\{1\})\P_{i,n}(\{0\})(\dot{\phi}_1(X_{i,n} eta_{\M,n}^*) - \dot{\phi}_2(X_{i,n} eta_{\M,n}^*))^2 \ \;&\le\; \sup_{|\gamma|\le K^*(	au,C)}(\dot{\phi}_1(\gamma) - \dot{\phi}_2(\gamma))^2, \end{align*} for the constant $K^*(	au,C)$ of Lemma~ef{lemma:pseudoBound}. Thus, the trace on the last line of display~\eqref{eq:lUnifCons:trace} is bounded by $p\max_{h\in\mathcal H}\sup_{|\gamma|\le K^*(	au,C)}(\dot{\phi}_1(\gamma) - \dot{\phi}_2(\gamma))^2$, which does not depend on $n$, $\M$ or $\P_n$. Finally, to bound the remaining probability, note that $L_n(y,\delta)$ is lower bounded by the product of $\lmin(U_{M,n}^{-1/2}H_{\M,n}^*(y)U_{M,n}^{-1/2})/n$ and $\inf_{ eta\in N_n(\delta)} \lmin(H_{\M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2}H_{\M,n}(y, eta)H_{\M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2})$. The first factor is itself lower bounded by the positive constant $\underline{K}(	au, C)$ from Lemma~ef{lemma:Hcontinuity}ef{l:Hcont:A}. Thus, $\P_n(L_n(\cdot,\delta) < \eps )$ is upper bounded by $$ \P_n\left( \sup_{ eta\in N_{n}(\delta)} \left\| H_{\M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2}H_{\M,n}(y, eta)H_{\M,n}^*(y)^{-1/2} - I_{m(\M)} ight\| > 1-  rac{\eps}{\underline{K}(	au, C)} ight). $$ Choosing $\eps = \underline{K}(	au, C)/2$ and using Lemma~ef{lemma:Hcontinuity}ef{l:Hcont:B}, we conclude that for every $\delta>0$,  egin{align} &\sup_{\M\in\mathsf{M}_n}\sup_{\P_n\in\mathbf{P}_n^{(\mathrm{bin})}(	au)} \P_n\left( \left\| (X_n[M]'X_n[M])^{1/2}(\hat{ eta}_{\M,n} -  eta^*_{\M,n}(\P_n))ight\| > \deltaight)\ &\quad\le \sup_{\M\in\mathsf{M}_n}\sup_{\P_n\in\mathbf{P}_n^{(\mathrm{bin})}(	au)} \P_n(E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta)^c)\ &\quad\le 16 rac{p\max_{h\in\mathcal H}\sup_{|\gamma|\le K^*(	au,C)}(\dot{\phi}_1(\gamma) - \dot{\phi}_2(\gamma))^2}{\delta^2\underline{K}(	au,C)^2} + o(1), \end{align} where the $o(1)$ term refers to convergence as $n	o\infty$. Now, to establish the asymptotic existence of the MLE, we simply take $E_{\M,\P_n,n} :=E_{\M,\P_n,n}(\delta_n)$, for $\delta_n	o\infty$ sufficiently slowly as $n	o\infty$. For the uniform consistency part, note that the limit superior as $n	o\infty$ of the expression in \eqref{eq:lUnifCons:sup} is bounded by a quantity that converges to zero as $\delta	o\infty$. \hfill{\qed}
